    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be given three points. A line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;, intersects lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> respectively. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the areas of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is equal to :",
